.TH YR-DUMP 1 "" YARA-X "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yr\-dump \- Show the data produced by YARA modules for a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fByr dump\fR [\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-module\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-colors\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the data produced by YARA modules for a file
.PP
YARA modules analyze files and extract information from them. This command shows all
the data produced by one or more YARA module for the given file. If no module is
explicitly specified with the `\-\-module` option, any module for which YARA produced
some information will be shown.
.PP
If the file is not provided it will be read from stdin.
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
yr dump \-\-module pe SOMEFILE
yr dump \-\-module pe \-\-module dotnet SOMEFILE
yr dump \-\-max\-depth 1 SOMEARCHIVE
cat SOMEFILE | yr dump
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 0]
Maximum container extraction depth

When <DEPTH> is 0, only the data produced by YARA modules for <FILE> itself is
shown. When <DEPTH> is greater than 0, supported container formats are recursively
unpacked up to <DEPTH> levels, and module data is dumped for both <FILE> and the
inner files extracted from it.

With <DEPTH> greater than 0, the output becomes a map keyed by file path
(<FILE> for the original file and <FILE>/<inner_path> for extracted files),
omitting any file for which no module produced meaningful data.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-module\fR
Module name
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
lnk
.IP \(bu 2
macho
.IP \(bu 2
elf
.IP \(bu 2
pe
.IP \(bu 2
dotnet
.IP \(bu 2
olecf
.IP \(bu 2
vba
.IP \(bu 2
crx
.IP \(bu 2
dex
.IP \(bu 2
zip
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-colors\fR
Turn off colors in YAML output
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Desired output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Path to binary file
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fByr\fR(1)
